<title>USA: Mothers Work Q2 net March 31 loss widens.</title>
<headline>Mothers Work Q2 net March 31 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second Quarter Ended   Six Months Ended</p>
<p>		    3/31/97	3/31/96     3/31/97	3/31/96</p>
<p> Net Sales   $55,755,776 $45,014,474 $116,989,104 $95,064,883</p>
<p>Restructuring</p>
<p>  Charges	5,617,094	   ---    5,617,094	   ---</p>
<p>Income Taxes</p>
<p>  (Benefit)  (3,103,413)    (71,211)  (2,359,945)   1,364,161</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)</p>
<p>		 (7,889,326)    (77,855)  (7,421,265)   1,501,724</p>
<p>Preferred Dividends</p>
<p>		     299,767     244,375	544,142     488,750</p>
<p>Net Income</p>
<p>Available</p>
<p>to Common</p>
<p>Stockholders</p>
<p>		 (8,189,093)   (322,230)  (7,965,407)   1,012,974</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss) Per</p>
<p>  Common Share    (2.30)	(0.10)	 (2.24)	  0.30</p>
<p>Weighted Average</p>
<p>Common Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding  3,563,342   3,123,170    3,561,306   3,365,362</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income was calculated before the payment of preferred dividends, earnings per share were calculated after the payment of preferred dividends.</p>
<p>Mothers Work Inc said its net income for the second quarter of 1997 includes restructuring charges of $7.6 million, or $1.40 per share, which consists of a $5.6 million charge to restructure and consolidate upscale maternity lines, a $0.8 million charge to write-down inventory related to this consolidation and $1.2 million to write-down long-lived assets at some of its continuing retail locations and for certain other costs.</p>
<p>Revenues increased primarily due to sales generated by Episode(R) America stores, acquired on June 1, 1996.</p>
